### 1. Architectural & Algorithmic Intuition
An **LRU (Least Recently Used) Cache** eviction policy requires two conflicting operations:
1. Fast key-value lookup (**O(1)** via Hash Map).
2. Fast deletion and re-insertion at the head of access order (**O(1)** via Doubly Linked List with dummy head and tail sentinel nodes).

### 2. Formal Proof of Correctness & Invariants
- **Sentinel Invariant**: `head->next` always references the Most Recently Used (MRU) node. `tail->prev` always references the Least Recently Used (LRU) node.
- **Capacity Invariant**: If `map.size() > capacity`, the node immediately preceding `tail` is unlinked and deleted in $O(1)$ operations.

### 3. Complexity & Boundary Analysis
- **Time Complexity**: **O(1) amortized** for both `get(key)` and `put(key, val)`.
- **Space Complexity**: **O(capacity)** strictly bounded memory allocation.

### 4. Production Polyglot Implementation
```cpp
// C++20 Production O(1) LRU Cache
#include <unordered_map>
#include <memory>
#include <mutex>

template <typename Key, typename Value>
class LRUCache {
    struct Node {
        Key key;
        Value value;
        Node* prev = nullptr;
        Node* next = nullptr;
        Node(Key k, Value v) : key(k), value(v) {}
    };

    size_t capacity_;
    std::unordered_map<Key, Node*> cache_;
    Node* head_;
    Node* tail_;
    mutable std::mutex mutex_;

    void attachToHead(Node* node) {
        node->next = head_->next;
        node->prev = head_;
        head_->next->prev = node;
        head_->next = node;
    }

    void detach(Node* node) {
        node->prev->next = node->next;
        node->next->prev = node->prev;
    }

public:
    explicit LRUCache(size_t capacity) : capacity_(capacity) {
        head_ = new Node(Key{}, Value{});
        tail_ = new Node(Key{}, Value{});
        head_->next = tail_;
        tail_->prev = head_;
    }

    bool get(const Key& key, Value& out) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        auto it = cache_.find(key);
        if (it == cache_.end()) return false;
        detach(it->second);
        attachToHead(it->second);
        out = it->second->value;
        return true;
    }

    void put(const Key& key, const Value& value) {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
        auto it = cache_.find(key);
        if (it != cache_.end()) {
            it->second->value = value;
            detach(it->second);
            attachToHead(it->second);
            return;
        }
        if (cache_.size() >= capacity_) {
            Node* lru = tail_->prev;
            detach(lru);
            cache_.erase(lru->key);
            delete lru;
        }
        Node* newNode = new Node(key, value);
        attachToHead(newNode);
        cache_[key] = newNode;
    }
};
```

### 5. Adversarial Stress-Test Matrix
- **Capacity 0 or 1**: Sentinels prevent `nullptr` dereference.
- **Duplicate Key Updates**: Mutating value without growing cache size.

